4. Tools and Technologies

1-Programming Language:

Java 8 or higher.
2-Database:

MySQL or SQLite for storing room details, guest information, and bookings.
3-User Interface:

JavaFX or Swing for creating a graphical user interface (GUI).
4-Libraries/Frameworks:

JDBC (Java Database Connectivity) for interacting with the database.
JUnit for testing the application.
Log4j for logging.
5-Development Environment:

IDE: IntelliJ IDEA or Eclipse.
Database Management: MySQL Workbench or SQLite Studio.


5. Database Design
5.1 Tables
Rooms Table

Column Name	Data Type	Description
room_id	INT	Primary Key, Unique identifier
room_number	VARCHAR	Room number
room_type	VARCHAR	Type of room (e.g., Single, Suite)
price	DECIMAL	Price per night
availability	BOOLEAN	Availability status (TRUE/FALSE)


Guests Table
Column Name	Data Type	Description
guest_id	INT	Primary Key, Unique identifier
name	VARCHAR	Full name of the guest
contact_details	VARCHAR	Contact info (Phone/Email)
address	VARCHAR	Address of the guest



Bookings Table
Column Name	Data Type	Description
booking_id	INT	Primary Key, Unique identifier
guest_id	INT	Foreign Key, references Guests
room_id	INT	Foreign Key, references Rooms
check_in_date	DATE	Check-in date
check_out_date	DATE	Check-out date
payment_status	VARCHAR	Payment status (Paid/Pending)



Payments Table
Column Name	Data Type	Description
payment_id	INT	Primary Key, Unique identifier
booking_id	INT	Foreign Key, references Bookings
amount	DECIMAL	Total amount
payment_date	DATE	Date of payment
status	VARCHAR	Status (Success/Failed)



6. Implementation Details
6.1 Admin Operations
Login: Admin can log into the system with a secure username and password.
Room Management: Admin can add, delete, or modify rooms using the Room class.
Booking Management: Admin can view current bookings and check-in/check-out guests.
Report Generation: Admin can generate reports such as the number of rooms booked and the total revenue.


6.2 Guest Operations
Room Booking: Guests can view available rooms and make bookings.
View Booking Details: After booking, guests can check the status and details of their reservation.
Payment Processing: Guests can pay for their stay using the Payment class.



7. Testing
7.1 Unit Testing
Unit testing will be done using JUnit to test individual methods and components such as booking functionality, guest registration, and payment calculation.

7.2 Integration Testing
Integration testing ensures that all components (UI, business logic, and database) work together seamlessly.

7.3 User Acceptance Testing
User Acceptance Testing (UAT) will involve real users testing the system to ensure it meets their requirements.



8. Conclusion
This Hotel Management System in Java aims to automate essential processes in hotel operations, 
offering a robust and scalable solution. By integrating features like room management, booking,
payment, and reporting, the system enhances operational efficiency while providing a smooth user experience.

This documentation provides a comprehensive overview of the project, its objectives, architecture, and implementation. With the system, hotels can streamline their operations and offer a better service to their customers.












